  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This private compatibility module only declares the legacy resource and\n selector address shapes; it has no handwritten executable code. Its derived\n serialization and identity operations do not emit source-line measurements.\n The source-tool argument and delivery regressions in `agent/tests.rs`\n exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter. Supported path-based\n address construction is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/resource.rs` (root) is valid.\n\n- **Built-in rules.** The built-in allows a file-root citation that gives a substantive prose reason in fenced commentary. This citation does that. It excuses only the file's coverage threshold.\n- **Claim: no handwritten executable code.** The file holds only `ResourceId` and `OutlineId`, two plain structs with derived `Clone`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Serialize` and `Deserialize`. This matches the current source.\n- **Claim: private compatibility module.** `lib.rs` declares `mod resource` privately when the `habeas-integration` feature is off. With the feature on, it is a `#[doc(hidden)] pub mod`. The commentary's \"private\" is therefore slightly loose, but this does not undermine the justification.\n- **Claim: `agent/tests.rs` exercises these addresses through the legacy adapter.** The source-tool tests in `agent/tests.rs` construct and observe `ResourceId` and `OutlineId`. Examples are `source_tools_keep_search_discovery_separate_from_delivered_source_reads`, `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery` and `source_tools_forward_arguments_and_present_discovery_and_read_results`. The production code that uses them is `agent/sources.rs`, in `SourceSession::dispatch`.\n- **Claim: path-based address construction is tested in `tests/outline_content.rs`.** `addresses_reconstruct_without_reading_the_file` tests `crate::outline::OutlineId` construction, a serialization round trip, selector validation and inequality.\n- **Redundancy.** The file's `{impl}` references name `requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses`, not `habeas:coverage`. The citation is therefore not redundant.",
